We propose \textbf{UP-VLA}, which unifies multi-modal understanding and future prediction in a single autoregressive backbone (Figure~\ref{fig:fig1}). It trains two complementary objectives---MMU from large-scale image-text data and PRE from robot video/action data---and fuses them via unified prompting and attention masking so that action generation conditions on both semantic scene descriptions and predicted visual futures.

