\textbf{Ablations.} Table~\ref{table:ablate} shows that removing prediction drops ABC$\rightarrow$D average length from 4.08 to 1.44, so prediction is crucial for spatial and dynamics grounding. Removing Bridge pre-training lowers it to 2.74, so predictive pre-training helps downstream performance. Removing MMU barely changes CALVIN (3.89) and real seen tasks (0.85) but cuts unseen-object success from 0.58 to 0.20, showing MMU is critical for semantic generalization; removing MMU conditioning gives 3.99 / 0.80 / 0.50, so conditioning actions on MMU-derived scene descriptions further helps.

